## 8. Limitations

{% set high_thr = [] %}{% for s in ['winter', 'spring', 'summer', 'fall'] %}{% if th24.performance[s].coverage_low|round(3) > nominal|round(3) %}{% set _ = high_thr.append(s) %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
- **Conditional coverage.** {% if sides.season.under or sides.decile.under %}The production interval under-covers {{ groups(sides.season.under, sides.decile.under) }} (section 4).{% if sides.season.under %} The coverage thresholds of {{ groups(sides.season.under, []) }} are drawn from weeks that already had that under-coverage: the monitor does not flag it as decay.{% endif %}{% else %}No season and no decile is under-covered in the sense of section 4.{% endif %}{% if high_thr %} The other way round, the coverage threshold of {{ groups(high_thr, []) }} ({% for s in high_thr %}{{ th24.performance[s].coverage_low|pct(1) }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}) is above the {{ nominal|pct(0) }} nominal: a week covered above nominal can be flagged low there. The thresholds measure departure from each season's validation coverage, not from nominal.{% endif %}{{ '' }}
- **Extreme cold.** {% if peak.evaluated == 0 %}No prediction interval covers the {{ peak.named_month }} peak{% elif peak.covered == 0 %}The {{ peak.named_month }} peak is not covered{% else %}The {{ peak.named_month }} peak is only partly covered{% endif %} ({{ peak.covered }} of the {{ peak.evaluated }} busiest hours){% if gaps|min > 0 %}; even with observed weather, the model under-forecasts it, and the cause is not tested{% endif %}. Only one peak is studied; cold snaps are not measured as a class.
{% set MEASURED = '(measured on ' ~ p.year ~ ', the year the rules were designed on, and on ' ~ r.year ~ ', out of sample, a measurement added after the results)' %}
- **Episodes of several days** {{ MEASURED }}. {% if E23.worst or E24.worst %}An episode of several days can yield "retrain" with nothing wrong in the model: {% else %}An episode is not a model failure: {% endif %}{{ episode_limit(E23, p.year, K.mild) }}; {{ episode_limit(E24, r.year, K.mild) }} (section 6).
- **Shift in level** {{ MEASURED }}. {{ level_limit(level, p.year, K.step_horizon) }} {{ level_limit(level24, r.year, K.step_horizon) }} {% set why = level_why([(p.year, level), (r.year, level24)]) %}{% if why|trim %}{{ why }} {% endif %}The power tables measure a gap between forecast and demand, not a shift in level.
- **Echo exclusion** {{ MEASURED }}. On a degraded model whose bias changes sides, it suppresses "retrain" on {{ p.year }} in {{ E23.echo.suppressed }} of {{ E23.echo.runs }} runs and delays it in {{ E23.echo.delayed }}, and on {{ r.year }} in {{ E24.echo.suppressed }} of {{ E24.echo.runs }} runs and delays it in {{ E24.echo.delayed }} (section 6); that is the price of avoiding the false alarms of an episode followed by its echo.
