## 10. Mapping to SR 11-7 and the NIST AI RMF

The quotations, with their sections and pages, are in `docs/standards.md`. The table says what the checks cover, nothing more.

| Expectation | What valiwatt does | Where it is checked |
|---|---|---|
| SR 11-7, conceptual soundness, including sensitivity analysis | Configuration fixed in the plan before validation (the temperature source after the data-quality report's comparison of stations on {{ span(K.design_years) }}); named features, coefficients shown beside a fit without the lags. Alternative specifications: the {{ dq.sources.eccc|length }}-station mean, absolute interval, one quantile per season, the first wording of rule 2. These are not the small changes in inputs and parameter values that SR 11-7 calls sensitivity analysis; those are not run. | Plan, section 2; validation and frozen-model runs |
| SR 11-7, data quality and relevance | {{ dq.checks.values()|selectattr('kind', 'equalto', 'gate')|list|length }} data-quality gates over the full window, each repair documented; the station's representativeness; in production, a daily data-quality monitor on the raw records. | Data-quality report; replays |
| SR 11-7, ongoing monitoring: process verification | Lookahead guards; a clock that refuses later records; the model's hash checked before and after; the {{ r.year }} replay refuses to run if the rules differ from the `rules-frozen` tag{% if departures %}; the tag was moved once, by a departure recorded in `AGENTS.md`, and the earlier replay is shown beside the new one (section 7){% endif %}. Each guard has its break. | Section 9 |
| SR 11-7, ongoing monitoring: benchmarking | Naive baseline; observed weather as an optimistic bound; frozen model against refitted folds on {{ p.year }} (a parallel outcomes analysis). | Sections 2 and 6 |
| SR 11-7, outcomes analysis and back-testing, with intervals | Monthly folds with embargo; {{ nominal|pct(0) }} intervals of split-conformal shape, without a finite-sample guarantee, with coverage measured overall, by season, by hour block and by decile; weekly statistics judged against thresholds fixed in advance. In SR 11-7's sense, a period not used in development, only the {{ r.year }} replay is back-testing: the validation years, {{ span(vy) }}, are among those ({{ span(K.design_years) }}) on which the station was chosen, and {{ p.year }} served to design the rules.{% if departures %} Since the departure, that back-test is the earlier replay, on the rules frozen before {{ r.year }} (section 7): the rules of the replay after the departure were changed after its results had been seen.{% endif %} | Sections 2, 4, 6, 7 |
| SR 11-7, thresholds of acceptability, then recalibration or redevelopment | Per-season thresholds from earlier weeks; an ordered decision table (investigate, retrain, recalibrate), with evidence; recommends without acting. | Sections 5 and 7 |
| SR 11-7, documentation and validation reports | This report and its model card, rendered from the runs and stamped with their IDs and the code hash. | This report |
| NIST MAP 2.2, 2.3 | Intended use, out of scope, weather caveat, limitations; validation design and data-quality findings documented. | Model card; plan |
| NIST MEASURE 1.1, 2.1, 2.3, 2.4, 2.5, 2.13 | MLflow runs (test sets, metrics, parameters, versions); replays under production conditions; breaks; the "not covered" list below. | Runs; section 9 |
| NIST MANAGE 2.2 | Weekly recommendations with evidence; who acts on them, and how, is out of scope. | Section 7 |

**Not covered.** Independent validation and effective challenge (SR 11-7, V; NIST MEASURE 1.3); governance, policies and controls, internal audit, model inventory (SR 11-7, VI; most of NIST GOVERN); periodic review; override analysis; use in decisions and materiality; independent review of a recalibration; sensitivity analysis in SR 11-7's sense (small changes in inputs and parameter values); NIST MANAGE 2.4 (who supersedes, disengages or deactivates the model); NIST MANAGE 4.1 and 1.4 beyond the model card's limitations; real-time data.

